  "text": "Skip to content\nSoren Hale\n01\nWork\n02\nServices\n03\nAbout\n04\nLab\n05\nWriting\nOpen to work from November\nGet in touch\n~\nServices\nDesign system\n\n// Service\n\nDesign system \n\nOne set of tokens and components your whole team actually uses.\n\nPrice\nFrom €12,000\nTimeline\n6 to 10 weeks\nStart this project\n\nOpens the contact form with this service picked. Nothing is sent yet.\n\n// Scope\n\nI build the system with your designers and the teams who will use it: tokens, accessible components, documentation and the process for changing it. Adoption is part of the job, not an afterthought.\n\nIncludes\n\nToken pipeline for code and Figma\nAccessible components with usage notes\nVisual and interaction tests\nMigration plan for existing screens\n\n// How it runs\n\nFrom the first note to the handover. \n\n01\nWeeks 1 to 2\n\nInventory\n\nEvery button, input and table that exists today, counted and grouped. The teams see their own drift on one page.\n\n02\nWeeks 3 to 4\n\nTokens\n\nColour, type and spacing in one file, generated for code and for the design library from the same source.\n\n03\nWeeks 5 to 8\n\nComponents\n\nBuilt in the order your teams need them, each with keyboard behaviour, a usage note and visual tests.\n\n04\nWeeks 9 to 10\n\nAdoption\n\nTwo real screens migrated with each team, a contribution guide and a weekly office hour that outlives me.\n\n// Questions\n\nAsked about this service. \n01\nWe already have a component library.\n\nGood. I start from it. Most systems need fewer components and better ones, not a rewrite.\n\n02\nDoes it work with our design tool?\n03\nHow do you get teams to use it?\n\n// Other services\n\nFrom €9,500\nFrontend build\nYour product's interface, from the first component to the production deploy.\nFrom €3,200\nPerformance audit\nA measured list of what is slow, why, and what each fix is worth.\nFrom €6,400 a month\nTeam embed\nA senior frontend developer inside your team, three days a week.\n\n// Start a project\n\nTell me what you are building. \n\nThree quick picks so the first reply is useful. You finish the message on the contact page.\n\n01\nWhat do you need?\n\nFrontend build\nPerformance audit\nDesign system\nTeam embed\nSomething else\n\n02\nRough budget\n\nUnder €5k\n€5–10k\n€10–25k\n€25k+\nNot sure yet\n03\nYour name or company\nbrief.ts\ndraft, not sent\nexport const brief = {\nkind: null // not picked yet,\nbudget: null // not picked yet,\nname: null // not picked yet,\n}\n\nBrief so far: nothing picked yet\n\nContinue to contact\n\nor write to hello@sorenhale.dev\n\nNothing is sent from this page. Your picks are kept in this browser tab and wait for you on the contact form.\n\nFooter\n\nFrontend developer, Oslo\n\nWrite to me\nhello@sorenhale.dev\n\nOpen to work from November\n\n// Site\n\nWork\nServices\nProcess\nReviews\nContact\n\n// About\n\nAbout\nResume\nStack\nUses\nNow\n\n// More\n\nLab\nWriting\nFAQ\nPrivacy\nTerms\nCookies\n\n// Elsewhere\n\nGitHub\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nLinkedIn\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\nBluesky\n↗\n(opens in a new tab)\n\nLocal time, Oslo\n17:01 CEST\n\n© 2026 Soren Hale. Written by hand in Oslo.\n\nSorenHale\n\nCreate a free website with Framer, the website builder loved by startups, designers and agencies.\n\nEdit Content",
